; THE WEST DOWNS — a transitional cell (the 2026-08-29 geography overhaul).
;
; ⚠️ IT IS ALMOST EMPTY AND THAT IS THE WHOLE POINT. Everything the player sees here — the ground,
; its elevation, its collision, the vegetation on it and the road across it — is authored in
; data/regions/EmberCrown.tres and built at load: the terrain mesh from the region heightfield,
; the ecology from the cell's biome scatter profile, the route from its path segments. A
; transitional cell costs one terrain draw and a handful of MultiMesh draws, which is what makes
; making the world five times larger cheaper per square metre rather than more expensive.
;
; Empty rolling grazing between the tarn country and the Crossway, with a drovers' track that
; crosses two rises and stops in the middle of a field.
;
; ⚠️ THE FOLD AT THE END OF THE TRACK, AND WHY A CELL WITH "NOTHING HERE" HAS FIVE NODES IN IT NOW.
;
; The drovers' track came off the warden compound, crossed two rises and stopped in the middle of a
; field. Empty country is the point of this cell and that has not changed - but a stopping PATH is
; not the same thing as empty country. A visible track is a promise, and one that pays out with
; literally no acknowledgement teaches the player that following a road is not worth the walk;
; after that every road in the realm is worth less, including the ones that go somewhere.
;
; So the track ends at a place rather than at a reward. Two courses of a collapsed sheepfold and a
; toppled boundary stone sit on the crest of the west rise, which is the highest ground in the cell:
; a player who walks out here gets the Crossway's palisade to the east, the tarn country falling
; away west, and an obvious answer to "why does this track exist". No loot, no interactable, no
; enemy, no map pin, no dialogue.
;
; ⚠️ DO NOT ADD A CHEST HERE. The moment one dead end pays out, every dead end has to.

; ⚠️ DO NOT FILL THIS IN. If a beat wants to happen here, the honest question is whether the realm
; needs another beat or whether this stretch is doing its job.

; ⚠️ THE NAV VOXEL GRID COARSENED WITH THE WORLD (the 2026-08-29 geography overhaul). Cells
; went from 52 m squares on a flat slab to 90-200 m of real terrain, and a 0.25 m voxel over
; five times the area is twenty-five times the columns to rasterise — the traversal probe timed
; out waiting for the bake. agent_* dims still sit on the voxel grid to avoid precision warnings.
